Z||000005||Rogue_Ant||08-05-2001||04:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Vlad:<BR><B><BR>Oil/filter - 2000 miles ago<BR>Rebuild distributor - one year ago.<BR>NGK plugs - one year/10K miles ago.<BR>Tranny oil/filter with flush - one month ago.<P>Other then described in first message problem, the car has some sort of trany problems. When it's hot and I come to complete stop at the traffic lights, there is a vibration and kind of BUZZing sound coming through TV cable to the throttle body. I actually can feel that vibration on the gas pedal.<BR>Another problem is that it eats oil. After a year of ownership, I still can't figure out where it goes. There is no leaks (no oil drips under the car) and no blue smoke. Nothing.....  However, I still have to add half litre of oil every 3 or 4 weeks (700-800 km).<BR>Go figure.......:-(<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What grade of oil are you using?  Possible that you have a small leak and just don't notice it?  Also check your mounts, that might be causing the vibration.<P>Rogue<P>||||reg||1
