Z||000007||Will||08-05-2001||11:28 AM||||Vibration:<BR>Do you have a miss at idle? That's about what frequency a miss would be at 600 RPM.<P>Hesitation:<BR>Try replacing the TPS. My car does the same thing. I think the TPS is bad, but the computer makes up for it with feedback from the O2 sensor in closed loop mode. But when it's cold in the morning the engine runs like crap until the O2 sensor warms up and the computer goes into closed loop mode.<P>Oil leak:<BR>Try checking the base of the distributor. There's an o-ring there which gets hard as a rock and ceases to seal.||||reg||1
